   1.000e-06     7.0421e-03     7.3723e-04      9.930e-01      9.993e-01      1.356e-03           NO
  [PASS] P2-1  at f = 1 the scalar is deeply Newtonian everywhere inside Saturn (y > 1e5, e^{-y} < 1e-40000): the analyticity hypothesis and hence the whole PPN expansion is EXACT there, with corrections far below any conceivable measurement -- so the symbolic beta result is valid in that corner
           (y(Saturn, f=1) = 5.433e+05, e^-y underflows to 0)
  [PASS] P2-2  *** at the Cassini-allowed coupling f = 1.15e-5 the scalar is in its OWN DEEP-MOND regime at Saturn (y << 1), so mu is NOT ~ 1, the e^{-y} corrections are NOT small, and the standard PPN expansion of this branch DOES NOT APPLY there. ***  Verifying the regime rather than assuming it is what exposes the problem.
           (y(Saturn, f=1.15e-5) = 8.495e-03  (needs >> 1 for PPN);  mu = 8.459e-03)
  [PASS] P2-3  the PPN expansion of this branch is valid out to Saturn (y > 30, e^{-y} < 1e-13) only for f >~ 7.43e-03.  This is a statement about the FORMALISM's own validity, entirely independent of any observational bound.
           (f_min(PPN valid at Saturn) = 7.431e-03)

