==============================================================================================================
PART 4 -- the KERNEL-INDEPENDENT anomaly theorem, and the perihelion gate
==============================================================================================================
  THEOREM.  If mu(y) <= y (true for every standard MOND kernel), then whenever the scalar is in its
  deep-MOND branch the scalar field obeys  f g_N = mu(y) g_s <= (f g_s/a0) g_s, i.e. g_s >= sqrt(a0 g_N).
  Hence the FRACTIONAL anomalous acceleration obeys      dg/g_N  >=  sqrt(a0/g_N)  -  f  ,
  and the scalar is deep-MOND (y<1) at radius r whenever  f < sqrt(a0/g_N(r)).

