==============================================================================================================
PART 5 -- an ABSORPTION-PROOF check: the radial run of the inferred GM_sun
==============================================================================================================
  A pure 1/r^2 anomaly would simply be absorbed into GM_sun.  The MOND-branch anomaly is 1/r, so the
  GM_sun inferred from each planet DRIFTS with r.  GM_sun is known to ~1e-10 fractionally.

    planet    a (AU)    GM_eff/GM - 1
   Mercury    0.3871       4.6627e-05
     Earth    1.0000       1.3370e-04
      Mars    1.5237       2.0817e-04
   Jupiter    5.2034       7.3158e-04
    Saturn    9.5371       1.3481e-03
  [PASS] P5-1  at f = 1.15e-5 the GM_sun inferred at Saturn exceeds that inferred at Mercury by 1.301e-03 (fractional), against a fractional knowledge of GM_sun of ~1e-10.  This is an ABSORPTION-PROOF inconsistency: no rescaling of GM_sun can hide a 1/r force.
           (GM_eff(Saturn)/GM_eff(Mercury) - 1 = 1.3014e-03   (~1.3e+07 x the GM_sun uncertainty))

